WEBVTT

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:06.240
Mitsuki-<i>san</i>!

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.020
We can ask Ichijo-<i>san</i>
what happened when she wakes up.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.710
We don't need to take her to a hospital?

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:25.290
I gave her first aid,
and her life's in no danger.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:27.630
Where are you going?

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:30.550
That storehouse. I'll get rid of the body.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:35.990
Um... Why are you investigating Ryuzoji?

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.010
I'll tell you later.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:43.180
You'll need to find out
at some point, after all.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:46.770
Take care of Ichijo-<i>san</i>.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.690
She's still under the
influence of Niarb. Be careful.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:51.400
Got it.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:00.990
This is a little different
from the other parallel worlds...

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:38.340
"Episode 13: An Ordained Fate"

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.140
You awake?

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:45.970
You were refusing to wake up,
so I was about to kiss you.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:48.640
Like a prince from a fairy tale, you know?

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:49.690
Where am I?

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:51.150
My bed...

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.310
That's what I'd prefer, anyway.

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.610
But unfortunately it's the nurse's office.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.840
What happened to me?

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:02.030
You got in an accident. In Ryuzoji's car.

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:03.510
An accident?

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:05.610
No! It's dangerous!

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:10.860
You hit your head. Take it easy.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:13.870
There might be some painkillers
in the first aid box.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:22.340
Not much more than band-aids, huh?

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:31.000
A power outage? Crap...

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:47.030
You're going to die, Takuya!

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:55.360
Well done.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:57.920
Thank you.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.630
Ryuzoji!

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:05.340
It's useless.

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:07.600
Don't even bother resisting.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:11.020
So you were controlling Mitsuki-<i>san</i>.

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:15.600
Looks like you've been
doing a lot of sniffing around.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.720
You, and her...

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.650
Eriko-<i>sensei</i>?

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:24.990
She and I are actually old acquaintances.

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:29.330
I thought I was safe after Abel's death.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:32.540
I didn't expect her to come after me...

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:33.800
Abel?

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.390
I should've kept my mouth shut.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:39.000
Ichijo-<i>kun</i>, show it to him.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.860
Yes, Sensei.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:47.930
Th-That's...

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:49.300
I knew it.

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:52.930
You seem to know what this jewel is.

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:58.520
Which means Kodai
gave you the Reflector Device.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:01.380
The thing I've wanted for so long...

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:07.450
You still know nothing 
of that device's power.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:13.200
Don't you think it should belong
to someone who knows its true value?

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:17.560
Now, where is it?

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:20.540
Maybe it's closer than you think!

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:36.140
You're going to die, Takuya!

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:37.510
I start from here?!

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:40.110
Stop it!

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:44.940
Wake up, Mitsuki-<i>san</i>!

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:47.830
Takuya...

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:51.200
You're so kind...

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.700
Mitsuki-<i>san</i>, you're okay now?

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:02.630
Stop it! Stop, please!

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:10.240
Takuya, you're going to die!

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:19.440
E-Eriko-<i>sensei</i>?

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:22.650
I came back because I heard a noise.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:24.690
I told you to be careful.

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:26.320
I know that!

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:28.900
That's why I came from 
another parallel world.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:33.340
I see. Looks like this route
was the right one, then.

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:36.910
Come on, just tell me.

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:39.500
What is Ryuzoji planning?

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.570
Why did he do this to Mitsuki-<i>san</i>?

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:45.750
Let's head to his mansion.

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:47.540
I'll tell you the details there.

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:10.740
Hey, is it okay to move
the body before the cops come?

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:13.470
I get it. But there's no time.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:19.460
Here we go.

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:21.710
What's up with that wall?

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:23.660
The coloration there is different, but...

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:25.980
Knock it down.

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:27.710
Me?

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:29.470
Please. Do it now.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:33.340
Trespassing. Moving a corpse.

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:36.100
And now property damage...

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:52.610
Human bones?

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:55.310
Look carefully. Notice anything?

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:58.410
I'm not sure what I'm looking at...

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.580
There's no torso?

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:03.420
Just limbs and a head!

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:08.930
No way...

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:10.630
That's right.

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:13.430
The monster that was seen
during the uproar about the curse...

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:18.890
It's Abel's body,
with Principal Ryuzoji's soul inside.

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:25.750
Right now Ryuzoji's body has
been taken over by something else.

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:29.070
Is that possible?

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:31.150
It is.

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:34.030
For an Eternal Dimensional Criminal.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:35.990
Beings of pure thought who travel

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:38.580
between different dimensions,
interfering with events there.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:44.710
Well, I'm sure it's asking a bit much
to think you'd believe me immediately.

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:49.870
At the time, I didn't know that
he was actually something else.

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:54.510
I've come this far. I believe you.

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:58.970
I was looking into Ryuzoji,
so I could arrest him.

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:02.760
Arrest him? Who are you?

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:08.850
A long time ago... well, in the future,
from your point of view...

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:11.320
There was a man named Abel.

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:16.510
He was a scientist, and he and his
assistant spent their days doing research.

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:18.410
--The two of them studied the science of events.
--Here

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:20.200
--The two of them studied the science of events.
--Thank you.

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:23.370
They researched the Tree of Vrinda.

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:36.880
A diagram showing all the potential events
that can result from a single cause.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:40.300
The nodes on the diagram
split like the roots of a tree,

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:43.020
stretching out according to a set of rules.

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:47.480
This sequence of events becomes
a new event cause in and of itself,

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:50.210
creating new sequences in turn.

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:52.870
This is where the parallel worlds come from.

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:56.330
Abel performed a certain experiment.

00:09:57.110 --> 00:10:01.010
He searched for the root of all
the events that have ever taken place.

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:07.040
It's too dangerous to go to the root!

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.750
Don't worry.

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:11.640
Only my mind will be traveling
backwards through the events.

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:13.490
But...

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:15.640
Don't worry.

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:20.220
I'll be fine if you're here with me.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:40.100
He's passed through 2⁵⁰ event splits.

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:42.430
Things are going well.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.700
He's reached the 6th layer.

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:53.210
Light...

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:56.260
Infinite events are passing me by...

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:02.970
He's reached the 4th layer.

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:06.330
What lies beyond...?

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:13.060
The truths of the universe!

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:23.160
What's this? No, Abel!

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:24.910
This isn't the truth!

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:42.890
No... these numbers...

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:44.850
An eternal dimensional criminal?

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:58.730
What is this thing? It's after Abel?

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:01.700
2⁹⁶ event splits passed.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:03.450
He's approaching the 1st layer.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:04.740
Abel, run!

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:06.700
You won't be able to make it back!

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:21.970
Abel!

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:25.260
Are you okay? What happened
to the dimensional criminal?

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:31.590
I'm just fine. Let's continue the experiment.

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:34.020
I'm so glad...

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:38.840
Who are you?

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:40.650
What's wrong?

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:45.990
No. You're... You're not Abel!

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:01.960
I've inherited all of this man's memories.

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:05.060
But you're not easily fooled, are you?

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:09.560
Especially if you love each other...

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:10.600
Abel.

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:13.430
This is a good body. I like it.

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:14.810
I'm taking it.

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:20.320
The eternal dimensional
criminal took Abel's body,

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:24.280
and fled to the parallel world we are in now.

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:28.550
And then he switched
from Abel's body to Ryuzoji's.

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:46.010
Abel's soul, stripped of its body,
is still wandering event space.

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:06.070
That tapestry always creeps me out..

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:10.670
This is the spot.

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:18.330
It's just up ahead.

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:33.130
What? The Reflector Device...

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:37.000
It's resonating with what's up ahead.

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:48.400
What is this?

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:51.240
A device that allows you
to move between parallel worlds.

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:55.200
It does the same thing 
as your Reflector Device.

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:56.540
It's broken.

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:59.230
It probably was destroyed
when he came to this dimension.

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:03.240
That's why he pretended
to be Ryuzoji and approached you.

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:07.130
An interesting theory,

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:11.020
except for the fact that 
it's complete fantasy.

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:13.400
Ryuzoji...

00:15:13.890 --> 00:15:18.390
The bones in the storehouse wall.
All that stuff about the curse.

00:15:18.390 --> 00:15:20.860
And this dimensional transportation device.

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:28.800
All these fragments point to one object.

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:31.410
You're under arrest!

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:35.910
You wanted to catch me so bad you
became a dimensional inspector?

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:39.000
Watch out!

00:15:57.640 --> 00:15:59.640
Wait, he doesn't die?

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:03.190
To a being of pure thought,
the body is just a vessel.

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:04.130
But...

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:08.440
There are limits to how 
much a vessel can take!

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:13.820
This is it!

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:19.040
Eriko-<i>sensei</i>!

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:26.210
It seems we have the upper hand now.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:33.720
Ichijo-<i>kun</i>, tie them up.

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:34.480
Yes, sir.

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:37.720
Is something wrong?

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:40.520
No. I'm fine.

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:41.890
I'll do it now...

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:44.020
Fool.

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:53.590
Mitsuki-<i>san</i>!

00:16:55.070 --> 00:16:57.280
This body won't last any longer.

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:01.500
Wait!

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:19.650
No... you were trying to protect me.

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:23.480
It's fine... It's okay now.

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:25.020
It is not!

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:26.960
You died because of me!

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:33.400
I was always thinking about you...

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:42.770
Hello?

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:49.700
Hello?

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:58.950
I always... loved you...

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:08.480
The jewel...

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:09.950
Take it.

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:12.980
I know you'll need it.

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:20.950
Takuya... keep following your path...

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:23.740
Without hesitation...

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:30.600
Mitsuki-<i>san</i>! Mitsuki-<i>san</i>!

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:34.300
Answer me! Please!

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:36.790
Mitsuki-<i>san</i>! Mitsuki-<i>san</i>!

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:49.780
It's useless.

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:55.690
Going to another parallel world
won't bring her back.

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:58.530
This conclusion was already ordained.

00:18:58.530 --> 00:19:00.030
What the hell does that mean?

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:03.230
It doesn't matter whether 
she was shot or not.

00:19:03.230 --> 00:19:05.240
The outcome would've been the same.

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:08.040
The flux in the event potential is too high.

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:14.520
You've experienced goodbyes
with her before, haven't you?

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:19.220
Forget about Mitsuki Ichijo.

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:21.800
She's going to disappear soon.

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:25.810
An event that cannot be avoided.

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:28.210
People call that "Fate."

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:31.400
So my saying goodbye to Mitsuki-<i>san</i> is fate?

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:32.400
Yes.

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:35.380
No matter what parallel world
you go to, that won't change.

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:40.530
No... I refuse to accept that!

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:45.280
Again?

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:47.790
The forced revision of causality.

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:49.320
The correction of chaos.

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:54.670
Just in case, I'll erase your
memories of me and Ryuzoji.

00:19:54.670 --> 00:20:00.460
If he thinks you know who he is,
he'll go after you even in another world.

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:02.090
Is that okay?

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:03.840
Yeah.

00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:13.150
What will you do when you get
to the new parallel world?

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:15.270
What I have to do.

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:18.530
No matter what fate awaits me,

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:22.190
I'll follow my path!

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:38.760
Takuya.

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:40.610
Dad...

00:20:41.050 --> 00:20:44.260
Causality guides everything.

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:49.600
I'm not interested in 
your lectures right now.

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:51.600
I'm just sick of all this.

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:56.270
Even if it's fate...
saying goodbye to the people I love...

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:05.110
The one that will show you
the path... is Kanna Hatano.

00:21:05.110 --> 00:21:06.620
Kanna-<i>chan</i>?

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:09.910
And when the eight jewels are gathered,

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:12.440
a new path will be opened to you.

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:14.750
A new path...

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:18.380
Takuya, I'll be waiting for you.

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:31.890
Here again, huh?

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:32.930
Oh, right...

00:21:37.150 --> 00:21:39.450
The same awful pain as always...

00:21:50.830 --> 00:21:52.090
Kanna-<i>chan</i>.

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:56.290
Now tell me about you.

00:21:57.500 --> 00:21:59.250
All about you...

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:41.480
"Episode 14: The Transfer Student's Friend"

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:39.390
Episode 14: "The Transfer Student's Friend."
